description:
Introduce an `NTT`-friendly field API. Needed by Task 7 (NTT multiplication); independent of Tasks 1–5.

## New module `crates/gf2-core/src/field/two_adic.rs`

```rust
pub trait TwoAdicField: FiniteField {
    /// The largest k such that 2^k divides |F*|.
    const TWO_ADICITY: u32;
    /// A fixed generator of the 2^TWO_ADICITY-th roots of unity.
    fn two_adic_generator() -> Self;
    /// The 2^k-th root of unity for k <= TWO_ADICITY. Panics if k > TWO_ADICITY.
    fn two_adic_root_of_unity(k: u32) -> Self {
        assert!(k <= Self::TWO_ADICITY);
        Self::two_adic_generator().pow(1u64 << (Self::TWO_ADICITY - k))
    }
}
```

## Impls

- `Fp<P>` (and specialised prime-field types via `gfp/specialized.rs`) for every supported Proth prime. `TWO_ADICITY = PrimeShape::Proth { n, .. }.n` extracted at compile time.
- Hard-coded primitive generators per supported prime in a small table — at minimum `Fp<65537>`, BabyBear, KoalaBear. Cite references in comments.
- **Explicitly NOT implemented** for `Gf2mElement_<V>`; multiplicative group has odd order `2^m - 1` so `TWO_ADICITY = 0` trivially. Document in module prose.

## Const-generic constraint (per breakdown doc risk #6)

`TWO_ADICITY` must be derivable from the const-generic `P`. If `const fn` in trait-const position requires nightly on MSRV 1.80, fall back to a helper `struct ProthConst<const P: u64>` with a `pub const TWO_ADICITY: u32` and have the `TwoAdicField::TWO_ADICITY` delegate to it. Document the workaround.

## Success criteria

- Unit tests per supported prime: `g = two_adic_generator()` satisfies `g^(2^TWO_ADICITY) == 1` and `g^(2^(TWO_ADICITY-1)) != 1` (primitive check).
- `cargo fmt` / `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` / `cargo test --release` clean.
- Every public item doc-commented with `# Arguments` / `# Examples` / `# Panics` / `# Complexity`.

